  - TYPE: File

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document states what the E2E protection must do: the CRC and alive counter that every message carries (ADR 0004, ADR 0007), how a sender writes them, and how a receiver checks them.
Each requirement links to the system requirements it serves; requirements without a parent are derived from a design decision.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_001
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e
TITLE: CRC algorithm
STATEMENT: The E2E CRC shall be CRC-8 SAE J1850: polynomial 0x1D, initial value 0xFF, final XOR 0xFF.
RATIONALE: The profile chosen in ADR 0007; known check values make it verifiable.
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_002
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e
TITLE: CRC coverage
STATEMENT: The E2E CRC shall be computed over the message ID as two bytes, low byte first, followed by payload bytes 0 to 6, and stored in payload byte 7.
RATIONALE: Including the ID detects a message that arrives with the wrong ID (ADR 0007).
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_003
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e
TITLE: Alive counter
STATEMENT: The sender shall write a 4-bit alive counter in the low nibble of payload byte 6, starting at 0, incrementing by 1 on every send and wrapping from 15 to 0.
RATIONALE: Lets the receiver detect lost and repeated messages (ADR 0007).
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_004
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e
TITLE: Protected bytes
STATEMENT: The sender shall leave payload bytes 0 to 5 and the high nibble of byte 6 unchanged.
RATIONALE: Signals live in those bits; protection must not overwrite them.
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_005
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e
TITLE: Corrupted message
STATEMENT: The receiver shall report a message whose CRC does not match as corrupted.
RATIONALE: Corrupted content must never be used.
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_006
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e
TITLE: Repeated message
STATEMENT: The receiver shall report a message whose counter equals the last accepted counter as repeated.
RATIONALE: A stale message repeated by a faulty sender must not be used as new data.
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_003
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_007
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e
TITLE: Lost messages
STATEMENT: The receiver shall accept a message whose counter is ahead of the last accepted counter by more than 1, modulo 16, and report the number of lost messages.
RATIONALE: The content is valid; the gap is reported so that lost messages are visible.
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_008
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e
TITLE: First message
STATEMENT: The receiver shall accept the first message with a valid CRC whatever its counter.
RATIONALE: There is no previous counter to compare with after start-up.
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_009
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e
TITLE: State after rejection
STATEMENT: The receiver shall keep its last accepted counter unchanged when it reports a message as corrupted or repeated.
RATIONALE: A rejected message must not move the reference used to check the next one.
VERIFICATION: Test
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SYS_MON_004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SW_E2E_010
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: e2e, derived
TITLE: No dynamic allocation
STATEMENT: The E2E functions shall not allocate memory dynamically.
RATIONALE: Derived from ADR 0005: they run inside the cycle.
VERIFICATION: Test, Inspection
